.TH uptime 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
uptime \- how long the system has been up
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uptime
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uptime
prints the time of day, how long since the machine booted, how many
users are logged in, and the load averages over the last 1, 5 and 15
minutes.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH NOTES
The uptime comes from the monotonic clock, so it is right even if the
time of day was set from the DS3231 or over the network after boot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR who (1),
.BR free (1),
.BR ps (1),
.BR date (1)
